meta {
  name: Get Supertrend
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/options/supertrend/TSLA261016C00360000?timespan=M5
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  timespan: M5
  ~count: 200
  ~bars: 50
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # Supertrend on an Option Contract

  Computes the Supertrend indicator per bar for ONE option contract, reusing the
  SAME SupertrendService (and app.supertrend length/factor) the stock endpoint uses.
  Inspection/validation only — no orders.

  ## Path
  - `{occSymbol}` — OCC option code, e.g. TSLA261016C00360000.

  ## Query
  - `timespan` — bar granularity (default M5). Native only (M1/M5/.../Y).
  - `count`    — bars to fetch (default = app.options.bar-count; option max 1200).
  - `bars`     — how many most-recent points to return (default 50; 0 = all).

  ## Response (200)
  { optionSymbol, length, factor, timespan, barsFetched,
    latestSupertrend, latestDirection (UP|DOWN), latestClose, returned,
    series: [ { timestamp, timestampEt, close, atr, supertrend, direction, flip } ] }

  ## Errors
  - `400` — invalid timespan, or not enough bars for the ATR length.
  - `502` — Webull market-data error (e.g. 403 if US_OPTION not subscribed).
  - `503` — no bars for the contract.
}
